WEBVTT

00:00:03.060 --> 00:00:04.230
<i>Spring.</i>

00:00:04.480 --> 00:00:07.060
<i>While the cherry blossoms of 
Kyoto were in full bloom...</i>

00:00:07.600 --> 00:00:10.980
<i>Others were flying high,
 enjoying the blossoms,</i>

00:00:12.410 --> 00:00:16.110
<i>but I was deep down in the dumps.</i>

00:00:17.390 --> 00:00:19.420
<i>Until that day I went down 
to Teramachi Sanjo,</i>

00:00:21.250 --> 00:00:23.250
<b>We appraise and buy the antiques you have hiding at home</b>

00:00:21.680 --> 00:00:23.250
<i>to the antique shop "Kura"...</i>

00:00:23.520 --> 00:00:25.500
<i>and met a certain someone.</i>

00:00:44.140 --> 00:00:45.460
Welcome.

00:00:57.030 --> 00:01:02.040
"Holmes and Zen Master Hakuin"

00:00:57.030 --> 00:01:02.040
Episode One

00:01:03.160 --> 00:01:04.540
Aoi-san.

00:01:04.540 --> 00:01:06.140
Is something the matter?

00:01:06.800 --> 00:01:07.710
Aoi-san?

00:01:07.710 --> 00:01:10.080
Oh, n-no...

00:01:10.080 --> 00:01:14.790
I was just thinking about the 
first time I came to this store.

00:01:14.790 --> 00:01:16.800
It's already been about two weeks.

00:01:17.070 --> 00:01:18.940
Time certainly flies, doesn't it?

00:01:18.940 --> 00:01:19.800
Yes...

00:01:19.800 --> 00:01:22.200
Um, I've finished my cleaning.

00:01:22.200 --> 00:01:24.560
Is there any other work I need to do?

00:01:25.150 --> 00:01:28.270
Let me see... I can't think of anything.

00:01:28.810 --> 00:01:31.100
Why don't we move on to lesson time?

00:01:31.640 --> 00:01:33.550
All right, Holmes-san.

00:01:37.140 --> 00:01:39.860
You always wear those gloves, don't you?

00:01:40.320 --> 00:01:44.580
People don't usually wear gloves 
when dealing with porcelain,

00:01:44.580 --> 00:01:46.580
since the feel of it is so important...

00:01:47.820 --> 00:01:50.080
But this is my style.

00:01:51.080 --> 00:01:52.590
What's this one?

00:01:53.300 --> 00:01:55.510
It's a Kokaratsu tea bowl.

00:01:55.510 --> 00:01:57.390
Please, take a close look at it to start.

00:02:03.010 --> 00:02:05.890
The art isn't very good, is it?

00:02:05.890 --> 00:02:10.820
Yes, and that's part of Kokaratsu's charm.

00:02:10.820 --> 00:02:16.150
They say that Kokaratsu is the final 
destination of the pottery lover.

00:02:16.770 --> 00:02:18.140
It's known for the hard clay

00:02:18.140 --> 00:02:22.900
that forms fine wrinkles on the unglazed 
portion of the foot as it's finished.

00:02:22.900 --> 00:02:25.700
These are known as "crinkled cloth wrinkles."

00:02:26.120 --> 00:02:29.120
Crinkled cloth wrinkles...

00:02:29.120 --> 00:02:31.560
You're so excited to learn, aren't you?

00:02:31.560 --> 00:02:34.460
Oh, no, I wouldn't say that...

00:02:35.160 --> 00:02:38.240
<i>This man's name is Yagashira Kiyotaka.</i>

00:02:38.240 --> 00:02:40.090
<i>Also known as Holmes-san.</i>

00:02:40.090 --> 00:02:42.970
<i>In the two weeks since 
I started working here,</i>

00:02:42.970 --> 00:02:47.100
<i>he's occasionally given me 
private lessons about antiques.</i>

00:02:47.600 --> 00:02:51.480
<i>This shop is a well-known, 
government-licensed appraiser.</i>

00:02:51.720 --> 00:02:56.690
<i>Yagashira Seiji-san is the owner, 
and his grandson, Holmes-san, is in training.</i>

00:02:56.690 --> 00:02:59.360
<i>The owner is always traveling 
around the world,</i>

00:02:59.360 --> 00:03:01.100
<i>so I haven't met him yet.</i>

00:03:02.370 --> 00:03:05.690
<i>Holmes-san's father, Takeshi-san, 
is officially in charge of the shop,</i>

00:03:05.690 --> 00:03:09.370
<i>but he leaves most of it 
to Holmes-san in practice.</i>

00:03:10.330 --> 00:03:11.250
Aoi-san.

00:03:11.750 --> 00:03:14.130
Have you gotten used to working here yet?

00:03:14.440 --> 00:03:16.750
Oh, yes! Thank you for asking.

00:03:17.240 --> 00:03:19.240
I'm glad to hear it.

00:03:19.240 --> 00:03:21.890
I need to hash some things 
out with my editor.

00:03:21.890 --> 00:03:23.940
You can handle things here, can't you?

00:03:23.940 --> 00:03:24.890
Yes!

00:03:26.380 --> 00:03:28.890
He really is a popular author, isn't he?

00:03:29.210 --> 00:03:32.520
And I'm left running the shop as a result.

00:03:34.660 --> 00:03:36.450
Oh, welcome!

00:03:36.450 --> 00:03:37.780
Welcome.

00:03:38.170 --> 00:03:40.540
I'd like to request an appraisal.

00:03:40.540 --> 00:03:41.600
You mind helpin' out?

00:03:41.600 --> 00:03:44.260
Not at all. Please have a seat.

00:03:46.560 --> 00:03:48.540
Well, well...

00:03:49.640 --> 00:03:53.350
My family's run a business 
in Kyoto for generations.

00:03:53.350 --> 00:03:56.630
Is this one of those Kizeto tea bowls?

00:03:56.630 --> 00:03:59.420
I ain't got any interest 
in tea bowls myself...

00:03:59.990 --> 00:04:04.180
<i>He showed me a Kizeto tea bowl
 in one of our previous lessons.</i>

00:04:04.600 --> 00:04:06.680
<i>But this one is...</i>

00:04:08.740 --> 00:04:11.950
I'm sorry to inform you, but this is a fake.

00:04:11.950 --> 00:04:13.940
Wh-What'd you say?!

00:04:14.650 --> 00:04:18.440
A genuine Kizeto typically 
has a glossy appearance,

00:04:18.440 --> 00:04:22.340
as though the clay has been coated with oil.

00:04:22.340 --> 00:04:24.580
It should have an overall
 sense of immaculacy.

00:04:25.100 --> 00:04:28.580
This item has no such feel to it.

00:04:29.120 --> 00:04:33.100
But beyond its appearance, a genuine 
Kizeto has a lightness when held.

00:04:33.100 --> 00:04:35.460
It wouldn't have this leaden heft.

00:04:36.160 --> 00:04:40.840
In addition, while this has the lustrous 
green of chalcanthite applied before firing,

00:04:41.350 --> 00:04:44.060
it's gone quite dusky.

00:04:45.060 --> 00:04:49.600
This is very clearly a counterfeit 
designed to look like a Kizeto.

00:04:50.000 --> 00:04:51.350
<i>Counterfeit?</i>

00:04:52.000 --> 00:04:55.350
A kid like you don't know 
what he's talkin' about!

00:04:55.950 --> 00:04:57.350
I <i>do</i> know.

00:04:57.980 --> 00:05:03.230
I think you brought that tea bowl in here,
 knowing that it was counterfeit.

00:05:04.800 --> 00:05:07.450
You said that you live in Osaka, didn't you?

00:05:07.930 --> 00:05:11.130
Why, then, did you go to the 
trouble of bringing your tea bowl

00:05:11.130 --> 00:05:13.520
to an antique shop in Kyoto?

00:05:13.520 --> 00:05:15.550
I-It just turned out that way!

00:05:15.550 --> 00:05:18.160
I happened to be in Kyoto 
an' decided to stop by.

00:05:18.160 --> 00:05:21.430
And after you had this tea bowl made,

00:05:21.430 --> 00:05:24.130
you employed the aid of a professional 
to have it distressed,

00:05:24.580 --> 00:05:30.340
which suggests extensive experience 
in the counterfeiting trade.

00:05:32.720 --> 00:05:36.520
That suit... Forgive my impertinence, 
but it doesn't fit you well.

00:05:37.060 --> 00:05:39.020
Your shoes are falling apart, too.

00:05:40.070 --> 00:05:44.640
You came to my shop specifically, 
then waited until my father left.

00:05:44.640 --> 00:05:49.880
You'd heard there was an inexperienced
 appraiser working in Teramachi Sanjo,

00:05:49.880 --> 00:05:52.030
and you thought that you could deceive me.

00:05:52.310 --> 00:05:53.790
Am I wrong?

00:05:54.230 --> 00:05:56.830
Ah, well... y'see...

00:05:56.830 --> 00:05:58.540
I'm sorry to inform you,

00:05:59.010 --> 00:06:00.980
but while I may be young,

00:06:00.980 --> 00:06:04.550
I ain't so green that I'd be 
fooled by this crude imitation.

00:06:05.540 --> 00:06:08.550
I-I'll let you off easy just this once!

00:06:09.520 --> 00:06:12.300
I'm the one lettin' <i>you</i> off easy...

00:06:13.300 --> 00:06:16.320
Shoot, that really got my goat...

00:06:16.320 --> 00:06:19.310
Aoi-san, could you cast 
some salt out the door?

00:06:19.720 --> 00:06:21.560
What? Salt?

00:06:21.560 --> 00:06:23.440
Yes. Salt, please.

00:06:23.440 --> 00:06:28.310
All I have is this boiled egg seasoning...

00:06:28.310 --> 00:06:30.260
Wouldn't that be kind of a waste?

00:06:33.520 --> 00:06:36.330
Yes, indeed. That would certainly be a waste.

00:06:37.350 --> 00:06:39.010
I thought so.

00:06:39.010 --> 00:06:41.730
Why don't we make ourselves some eggs, then?

00:06:41.730 --> 00:06:42.650
Okay!

00:06:43.750 --> 00:06:45.050
Delicious!

00:06:45.050 --> 00:06:48.740
I really enjoy how disarming 
you are, Aoi-san.

00:06:48.740 --> 00:06:50.720
What do you mean?

00:06:51.070 --> 00:06:53.920
After dealing with a miserable counterfeit,

00:06:53.920 --> 00:06:56.930
I tend to spend the rest of the 
day feeling annoyed about it.

00:06:56.930 --> 00:07:01.120
But when I saw you there 
holding that seasoning,

00:07:01.120 --> 00:07:03.040
it was as if the whole thing deflated.

00:07:04.290 --> 00:07:06.100
I was honestly surprised myself...

00:07:06.100 --> 00:07:09.500
You really get people 
bringing in counterfeits?

00:07:09.500 --> 00:07:15.090
Counterfeits are a malicious practice 
designed to extort money from people.

00:07:15.090 --> 00:07:18.370
I cannot brook such evil.

00:07:18.970 --> 00:07:21.980
To those who love art, it's blasphemy.

00:07:24.000 --> 00:07:27.470
Holmes-san, you're a very 
upright person, aren't you?

00:07:27.470 --> 00:07:30.620
Upright? Me?

00:07:30.620 --> 00:07:31.500
Yes.

00:07:32.280 --> 00:07:35.290
No, I just hate counterfeits.

00:07:35.290 --> 00:07:39.430
I'm actually quite perverse, with 
a fundamentally wicked personality.

00:07:39.430 --> 00:07:40.740
Wicked?

00:07:41.530 --> 00:07:45.950
<i>It did sort of feel like he had
 a dark side to him back there...</i>

00:07:46.870 --> 00:07:49.400
<i>No, that can't be!</i>

00:07:49.400 --> 00:07:51.980
<i>After all, the day I first came here...</i>

00:07:55.620 --> 00:07:57.660
<b>Two Weeks Earlier</b>

00:08:03.880 --> 00:08:05.610
<i>Wh-What should I do?</i>

00:08:05.610 --> 00:08:08.150
<i>It's so hard to break the ice...</i>

00:08:09.800 --> 00:08:11.270
Welcome.

00:08:11.270 --> 00:08:13.560
Holmes! You mind havin' a look at this?

00:08:13.560 --> 00:08:17.300
Ueda-san, I must ask that you
stop calling me "Holmes."

00:08:17.300 --> 00:08:20.810
Aw, don't be such a spoilsport, now!

00:08:18.390 --> 00:08:20.810
<i>Holmes-san?</i>

00:08:21.520 --> 00:08:22.810
Well, well...

00:08:23.500 --> 00:08:24.560
<i>Amazing!</i>

00:08:25.000 --> 00:08:28.000
Yokoyama Taikan's 
"Mt. Fuji and Cherry Blossoms."

00:08:28.000 --> 00:08:30.010
It's a very fine piece.

00:08:30.010 --> 00:08:33.080
Right? And in real great condition, see?

00:08:33.080 --> 00:08:36.570
And a Yokoyama Taikan, to boot! 
It's gotta be worth a bundle!

00:08:37.030 --> 00:08:41.270
I see. It is very beautiful, 
and it is in very fine condition,

00:08:41.270 --> 00:08:43.870
but I regret to inform you 
that it's a reproduction.

00:08:43.870 --> 00:08:46.440
Aw, drat. It ain't the real deal, huh?

00:08:46.440 --> 00:08:48.210
<i>But it's so beautiful...</i>

00:08:48.480 --> 00:08:50.660
Okay, I hear you.

00:08:50.660 --> 00:08:52.550
I was hopin', just maybe...

00:08:52.550 --> 00:08:55.340
<i>He just took that clerk at his word...</i>

00:08:55.620 --> 00:08:58.470
<i>Even though he's so young...</i>

00:08:59.320 --> 00:09:04.120
<i>But there's so much passion in the 
selection and decoration of this shop.</i>

00:09:05.170 --> 00:09:06.780
<i>I don't know much about this kind of stuff,</i>

00:09:06.780 --> 00:09:08.230
<i>but they certainly seem like quality items...</i>

00:09:18.990 --> 00:09:20.240
What's this?

00:09:20.240 --> 00:09:22.040
Do you like it?

00:09:22.040 --> 00:09:28.470
Oh... I-I don't know. It just seemed... nice.

00:09:28.470 --> 00:09:32.330
I see. Please feel free to 
take your time browsing.

00:09:32.330 --> 00:09:34.240
E-Excuse me...

00:09:35.360 --> 00:09:36.130
Yes?

00:09:37.200 --> 00:09:40.140
Why did that man call you Holmes-san?

00:09:43.520 --> 00:09:47.460
Is it because you know lots of 
things, like Sherlock Holmes?

00:09:48.140 --> 00:09:49.900
Let me see...

00:09:50.340 --> 00:09:52.690
You're a student at Ohki High School.

00:09:52.690 --> 00:09:55.000
You originally came from eastern Japan.

00:09:55.000 --> 00:09:58.540
It's been about six months 
since you moved to Kyoto.

00:09:58.540 --> 00:10:02.190
You came to this shop because there's 
something you want to have appraised...

00:10:02.960 --> 00:10:06.280
But it's not something that belongs to you.

00:10:06.280 --> 00:10:09.010
How did you know I moved here six months ago?

00:10:09.010 --> 00:10:10.610
Just instinct.

00:10:10.610 --> 00:10:13.300
You don't seem as though
 you're too new in town,

00:10:13.640 --> 00:10:16.550
but you also don't appear 
to be completely at home.

00:10:16.550 --> 00:10:20.910
So I suspected you might have moved here 
during summer vacation last year.

00:10:20.910 --> 00:10:26.430
W-Well... how did you know that what I 
want appraised isn't really mine?

00:10:27.170 --> 00:10:32.060
High school students don't tend to own 
the kinds of things we appraise here.

00:10:32.060 --> 00:10:34.950
Moreover, your apparent hesitance 
to have it appraised

00:10:34.950 --> 00:10:38.070
suggests it doesn't belong to you.

00:10:38.600 --> 00:10:39.640
Am I wrong?

00:10:39.640 --> 00:10:41.800
W-Well...

00:10:41.800 --> 00:10:45.800
But you need money...

00:10:46.830 --> 00:10:51.330
So you took it out of the 
house without permission.

00:10:51.650 --> 00:10:53.340
Would that be correct?

00:10:54.120 --> 00:10:59.170
Kiyotaka, you're scarin' the girl. 
Knock it off already, would ya?

00:10:59.170 --> 00:11:01.840
This is why we call you Holmes.

00:11:02.520 --> 00:11:04.350
Forgive me. I let myself get carried away.

00:11:04.950 --> 00:11:08.020
<i>So they </i>do<i> call him Holmes 
because he knows everything...</i>

00:11:08.020 --> 00:11:11.760
Actually, Holmes is just a nickname.

00:11:12.690 --> 00:11:14.730
<i>D-Did he just read my mind?</i>

00:11:15.280 --> 00:11:17.480
My surname is Yagashira.

00:11:16.550 --> 00:11:21.260
<b>Ya{top right}</b>

00:11:16.800 --> 00:11:21.260
<b>Gashira{bottom left}</b>

00:11:17.480 --> 00:11:19.620
My full name is Yagashira Kiyotaka.

00:11:20.380 --> 00:11:22.360
It's written with the characters 
for "home" and "head" (zu),

00:11:22.360 --> 00:11:24.240
which resulted in the nickname
 Home-zu, or Holmes.

00:11:22.820 --> 00:11:24.240
<b>Holmes</b>

00:11:25.350 --> 00:11:27.990
I see, so that's where 
Holmes-san comes from...

00:11:27.990 --> 00:11:30.100
Kiyotaka-chan's just amazin'!

00:11:30.100 --> 00:11:33.630
He'll be goin' to Kyoto University 
for graduate school this spring.

00:11:33.960 --> 00:11:35.350
Kyoto University?

00:11:35.350 --> 00:11:39.410
I couldn't pass the entrance exam, 
so I'm transferring from Kyoto Prefectural.

00:11:39.410 --> 00:11:43.400
Kyoto University is relatively 
easy to get in to as a graduate.

00:11:43.400 --> 00:11:47.010
But I'll still be able to put 
"Kyoto University" on my résumé!

00:11:47.010 --> 00:11:49.210
<i>S-Seems a little dishonest...</i>

00:11:49.210 --> 00:11:51.080
Were you just thinking 
that it seems dishonest?

00:11:51.080 --> 00:11:52.520
N-No!

00:11:52.520 --> 00:11:55.520
<i>Scary! He really is like Sherlock Holmes!</i>

00:11:55.520 --> 00:11:57.900
So? What's your name?

00:11:59.440 --> 00:12:00.900
Mashiro Aoi.

00:12:00.900 --> 00:12:02.460
Aoi-san?

00:12:02.920 --> 00:12:04.830
What a lovely name.

00:12:05.780 --> 00:12:07.610
Do you live in Sakyo Ward?

00:12:08.050 --> 00:12:11.040
I'm originally from Saitama, 
but I do live there now.

00:12:11.040 --> 00:12:13.790
Close to Shimogamo Shrine?

00:12:13.790 --> 00:12:17.170
Th-That's right... How did you know?

00:12:18.050 --> 00:12:20.480
Heck, what a question...

00:12:20.480 --> 00:12:22.630
When you think of "Aoi," y'know...

00:12:22.630 --> 00:12:24.750
Anyway...

00:12:26.860 --> 00:12:32.060
Aoi-san, I can't buy things 
from people under 20 years old.

00:12:32.290 --> 00:12:35.500
I... I see.

00:12:35.500 --> 00:12:38.940
But I can still appraise them.

00:12:38.940 --> 00:12:41.440
Would you like to show me what you have?

00:12:41.920 --> 00:12:45.880
Anything you brought in would 
have to be something special.

00:12:46.720 --> 00:12:49.430
<i>Anything I brought in?</i>

00:12:49.430 --> 00:12:52.520
I could make some coffee. 
Would you like some?

00:12:52.520 --> 00:12:55.380
With sugar and milk, please!

00:12:55.950 --> 00:12:58.730
Then why don't I make some café au lait?

00:13:01.360 --> 00:13:02.960
Delicious...

00:13:03.980 --> 00:13:07.100
<i>Holmes-san doesn't speak with an accent.</i>

00:13:07.100 --> 00:13:09.970
<i>I wonder where he's originally from.</i>

00:13:10.300 --> 00:13:13.120
Oh, I've lived in Kyoto my whole life.

00:13:13.120 --> 00:13:16.080
I'm sure that's hard to tell when 
I'm speaking politely, though.

00:13:17.300 --> 00:13:19.020
<i>A-Again?</i>

00:13:21.670 --> 00:13:24.900
Um, do you always do that?

00:13:24.900 --> 00:13:30.440
No, I'm usually very careful not 
to not say everything I'm thinking.

00:13:30.440 --> 00:13:32.910
I wonder why today is different.

00:13:33.820 --> 00:13:34.750
This is...

00:13:36.130 --> 00:13:38.380
A zenga painting from Hakuin Ekaku.

00:13:38.380 --> 00:13:39.750
This is quite a surprise...

00:13:40.020 --> 00:13:41.750
It's genuine.

00:13:42.160 --> 00:13:44.760
Hakuin... Ekaku?

00:13:45.250 --> 00:13:47.840
A Zen Buddhist monk who lived 
in the mid-Edo period.

00:13:47.840 --> 00:13:50.000
He was known as the reviver 
of the Rinzai school.

00:13:50.000 --> 00:13:52.260
This daruma painting is 
in very fine condition...

00:13:52.460 --> 00:13:54.650
It's quite incredible.

00:13:54.650 --> 00:13:58.720
If you sold it... I believe it 
might fetch about two million yen.

00:13:58.720 --> 00:14:00.020
T-Two million?

00:14:00.520 --> 00:14:02.830
I'll have a look at the second one now.

00:14:03.900 --> 00:14:07.280
I think that one's by the same person.

00:14:07.280 --> 00:14:09.020
Though it's not a daruma...

00:14:10.250 --> 00:14:11.230
Um...

00:14:14.240 --> 00:14:16.070
I'm stunned...

00:14:16.070 --> 00:14:21.010
I've seen Hakuin draw infants before,

00:14:21.010 --> 00:14:23.670
but I've never seen this particular one.

00:14:24.000 --> 00:14:25.920
Is it that amazing?

00:14:25.920 --> 00:14:31.180
Yes. I don't think I could put a price on it.

00:14:32.840 --> 00:14:36.680
Aoi-san, to whom do these 
hanging scrolls belong?

00:14:41.550 --> 00:14:43.690
My late grandfather.

00:14:43.690 --> 00:14:47.530
He liked antiques, so he collected all kinds.

00:14:47.530 --> 00:14:49.200
I see...

00:14:49.480 --> 00:14:55.700
I'm sure you're not usually the kind of girl 
to steal family treasures and sell them off.

00:14:56.340 --> 00:14:58.420
And yet, here you are.

00:14:59.030 --> 00:15:03.000
That suggests that you've found 
yourself in truly dire straits.

00:15:04.080 --> 00:15:11.340
If I may be so forward as to ask, 
what could you need money for so badly

00:15:11.860 --> 00:15:14.570
that you would steal your 
grandfather's antiquities?

00:15:21.980 --> 00:15:23.860
I need a train ticket.

00:15:24.470 --> 00:15:29.210
Because I want... to go back to Saitama.

00:15:29.860 --> 00:15:32.610
Has something happened to you?

00:15:33.620 --> 00:15:39.930
Last month, the boy I was dating... 
said he wanted to break up.

00:15:41.050 --> 00:15:45.500
At the time, I thought, "Well, of course."

00:15:46.220 --> 00:15:48.720
He lives in Saitama, 
so we rarely saw each other.

00:15:48.720 --> 00:15:51.390
I thought it was only natural
 that we drifted apart...

00:15:52.520 --> 00:15:56.960
But he started dating another 
girl right after that.

00:15:57.480 --> 00:15:59.090
And the girl he started dating was...

00:16:00.790 --> 00:16:03.720
It was really sad and
hard for me, but...

00:16:04.300 --> 00:16:06.900
I see. And so...

00:16:06.900 --> 00:16:09.430
I want to give them a piece of my mind!

00:16:09.430 --> 00:16:13.800
To tell them they were awful!
 That I'll never forgive them!

00:16:13.800 --> 00:16:18.540
Because it's just so cruel... It's too cruel!

00:16:24.470 --> 00:16:25.580
Aoi-san.

00:16:26.590 --> 00:16:30.940
Please have a look at the picture 
of the baby you brought in.

00:16:31.740 --> 00:16:33.890
The picture?

00:16:36.200 --> 00:16:40.200
"In Suruga, there are two great abundances:

00:16:40.200 --> 00:16:42.810
the mountain of Fuji and the 
white-cloaked (hakuin) fields."

00:16:43.240 --> 00:16:45.640
That's what Hakuin was named after.

00:16:45.640 --> 00:16:48.700
But not even his life was without scandal.

00:16:49.440 --> 00:16:54.820
Once, the daughter of one of Hakuin's 
parishioners became pregnant.

00:16:55.360 --> 00:16:58.640
He interrogated her about who 
the father was. Too afraid to tell him,

00:16:58.640 --> 00:17:01.200
she lied and said that it was Hakuin's child.

00:17:01.850 --> 00:17:04.460
The parishioner was outrageously angry.

00:17:04.460 --> 00:17:09.460
He called Hakuin a degenerate monk 
and left the child in his care.

00:17:10.210 --> 00:17:14.970
Hakuin merely took the child in without 
speaking a word in his own defense.

00:17:14.970 --> 00:17:16.970
It is said that he walked around town,

00:17:16.970 --> 00:17:19.920
enduring the townspeople's abuse, 
to find for a woman to nurse the child.

00:17:19.920 --> 00:17:23.290
When the girl heard about this,
 she confessed the truth.

00:17:23.290 --> 00:17:27.130
The parishioner went to Hakuin 
and apologized profusely.

00:17:27.130 --> 00:17:28.730
Hakuin merely responded,

00:17:29.000 --> 00:17:34.180
"Is that so? It's good that 
the child has a father."

00:17:34.180 --> 00:17:39.520
He gave the baby back without a single 
ill word for the parishioner or his daughter.

00:17:40.270 --> 00:17:44.570
How do you think Hakuin felt at the time?

00:17:47.410 --> 00:17:50.560
He was betrayed and abused...

00:17:50.560 --> 00:17:53.330
but despite that, he tried his 
best to to raise the baby.

00:17:54.050 --> 00:17:59.390
So how did he feel when he was 
asked to give the baby back?

00:18:00.120 --> 00:18:04.460
He must have been angry about 
how selfish they were being...

00:18:05.250 --> 00:18:06.610
I wonder.

00:18:07.130 --> 00:18:11.650
Do you think we might find the way 
he felt reflected in this picture?

00:18:12.840 --> 00:18:14.210
In this picture?

00:18:23.120 --> 00:18:25.060
You can see it too, can't you, Aoi-san?

00:18:25.610 --> 00:18:28.560
Hakuin's love for the child.

00:18:28.560 --> 00:18:33.140
And his feelings of acceptance 
of and love for everything.

00:18:36.970 --> 00:18:38.170
Yes...

00:18:39.510 --> 00:18:44.370
I'm ashamed of how bitter and spiteful I was.

00:18:44.880 --> 00:18:50.660
I was going to sell this wonderful 
treasure just to go tell someone off...

00:18:51.580 --> 00:18:53.760
I really am ashamed of myself.

00:18:54.600 --> 00:18:55.940
Aoi-san.

00:18:55.940 --> 00:18:59.450
Would you like to come and work with me here?

00:19:01.650 --> 00:19:04.780
You appear to have a very good eye.

00:19:04.780 --> 00:19:08.710
Why don't you work here and 
earn the money for your ticket?

00:19:09.640 --> 00:19:11.710
B-But...

00:19:12.020 --> 00:19:15.710
When you have enough money for the trip, 
if you still want to go back to Saitama,

00:19:15.710 --> 00:19:18.970
you can go and get everything 
off your chest then.

00:19:23.960 --> 00:19:25.220
O-Okay.

00:19:25.480 --> 00:19:28.790
I accept your offer.

00:19:28.790 --> 00:19:30.100
I'm so glad.

00:19:31.120 --> 00:19:34.930
I've actually been looking 
for someone to help me out.

00:19:37.200 --> 00:19:39.490
When I remember how you acted that day,

00:19:39.870 --> 00:19:41.740
I find it hard to believe that you're wicked.

00:19:41.740 --> 00:19:43.520
Is that so?

00:19:43.520 --> 00:19:46.740
Maybe I was just pleased 
to find a gullible part-timer

00:19:47.350 --> 00:19:49.570
that I could manipulate for my own ends.

00:19:49.570 --> 00:19:52.230
I-I'm sure that's not the case!

00:19:52.750 --> 00:19:58.010
But, um, why did you say 
I have a good eye that day?

00:19:59.150 --> 00:20:00.680
Because...

00:20:00.680 --> 00:20:03.840
That tea bowl that caught your attention
 when you first came...

00:20:04.110 --> 00:20:06.350
That's a Shino tea bowl.

00:20:06.350 --> 00:20:08.030
A Shino tea bowl?

00:20:08.030 --> 00:20:09.870
It's one of my grandfather's 
most prized possessions.

00:20:09.870 --> 00:20:12.230
A national treasure from the Momoyama era.

00:20:12.480 --> 00:20:15.870
It's a masterpiece the likes of which
 will never be made again.

00:20:16.560 --> 00:20:19.810
If I had to put a price tag on it, 
I would say it's worth about 60 million yen.

00:20:19.810 --> 00:20:21.670
S-Sixty million?!

00:20:21.670 --> 00:20:24.240
You have something that 
amazing in a place like this?!

00:20:24.240 --> 00:20:27.000
It's our little secret.

00:20:27.000 --> 00:20:29.060
Hey there, Kiyotaka.

00:20:29.060 --> 00:20:31.750
Having some fun with a lady friend?

00:20:32.270 --> 00:20:33.550
Owner...

00:20:34.640 --> 00:20:38.560
This is Mashiro Aoi-san. 
She's helping out at the shop.

00:20:38.560 --> 00:20:40.310
I told you over the phone, remember?

00:20:40.310 --> 00:20:42.320
Ah, that's right. You did.

00:20:42.320 --> 00:20:46.880
Aoi-san, my grandson is a bit eccentric, 
but please look after him.

00:20:46.880 --> 00:20:51.520
Oh, he's really the one looking after... me?

00:20:51.840 --> 00:20:53.420
Aren't you a charmer!

00:20:53.420 --> 00:20:55.960
Why don't we grab some coffee together?

00:20:55.960 --> 00:20:57.020
What?

00:20:57.580 --> 00:21:00.900
Owner, please stop hitting on the part-timer.

00:21:01.320 --> 00:21:04.910
Now, did you have a reason for stopping by?

00:21:04.910 --> 00:21:06.660
Yes, that's right.

00:21:07.360 --> 00:21:12.170
There've been some convincing counterfeits 
making the rounds in antique shops lately.

00:21:13.350 --> 00:21:14.790
Take care, you hear?

00:21:14.790 --> 00:21:17.320
Oh, those?

00:21:17.320 --> 00:21:19.980
I actually just turned one of them away.

00:21:22.280 --> 00:21:26.400
It's lookin' like we can't 
afford to be careless...

00:21:28.640 --> 00:21:30.970
Yagashira Kiyotaka.

00:21:32.040 --> 00:21:34.420
I'll remember that name.

00:21:35.140 --> 00:21:36.900
I should be going now.

00:21:36.900 --> 00:21:39.320
Yes. It's getting dark.

00:21:39.320 --> 00:21:41.250
Take care on your way back to Shimogamo.

00:21:41.250 --> 00:21:42.100
Okay!

00:21:43.220 --> 00:21:46.630
How did you know I lived in Shimogamo?

00:21:46.630 --> 00:21:50.810
I'm sure you'll find that out soon enough.

00:21:53.680 --> 00:21:56.870
Are all Kyoto boys nasty?

00:21:56.870 --> 00:22:00.070
You weren't aware, Aoi-san?

00:22:01.720 --> 00:22:05.210
Us Kyoto boys... are awful nasty.

00:22:10.880 --> 00:22:13.440
<i>A wicked Kyoto boy, huh?</i>

00:22:14.990 --> 00:22:19.730
<i>At an antique shop called Kura 
in Kyoto's Teramachi Sanjo area,</i>

00:22:20.170 --> 00:22:23.840
<i>you'll find a mysterious 
Kyoto boy named Holmes.</i>

00:22:26.440 --> 00:22:31.020
<i>This is the tale of Holmes, 
AKA Yagashira Kiyotaka...</i>

00:22:33.210 --> 00:22:35.860
<i>Myself, Mashiro Aoi...</i>

00:22:37.830 --> 00:22:41.380
<i>And the quiet and beautiful story
of the cases we solved in Kyoto.</i>

00:22:42.290 --> 00:22:48.340
<b>Holmes of Kyoto</b>

00:23:36.390 --> 00:23:51.400
Next Episode

00:23:36.390 --> 00:23:51.400
"In Days of Aoi"

00:23:37.560 --> 00:23:41.400
Holmes-san, I think the Saio-Dai 
has gotten mixed up in a case.

00:23:41.400 --> 00:23:45.300
I see. I hope it doesn't become 
anything too troubling.

00:23:46.140 --> 00:23:48.440
Next time: "In Days of Aoi."

00:23:48.440 --> 00:23:58.440
Holmes-san, you really are nasty.
